  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/reconstruction-era> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The period from roughly 1863 to 1877 when the United States reunited the former Confederate states and tried, through new laws, three constitutional amendments and federal enforcement, to turn about four million freed people into citizens and voters, an experiment in interracial democracy that was overthrown by white-supremacist violence and Northern retreat." .
