  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Underground Road" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/african-american-history> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/resistance-to-slavery> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The resistance to slavery through escape and flight, from the late eighteenth century through the end of the Civil War, in which enslaved African Americans freed themselves, often with help from free and enslaved Black people and interracial local networks, and reached free states, Canada, Mexico and other refuges." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/civil-war-and-reconstruction> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/underground-railroad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Underground Railroad" .
