  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/second-continental-congress> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The assembly of delegates from the thirteen colonies that convened in Philadelphia on May 10, 1775, after fighting had begun in Massachusetts, and served as the de facto national government of the United States — raising the Continental Army, declaring independence and drafting the Articles of Confederation — until the Articles took effect on March 1, 1781." .
