  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/presidency-of-the-united-states> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The office at the head of the executive branch of the U.S. federal government, created by Article II of the Constitution, whose holder serves a four-year term as head of state, chief executive and commander in chief; George Washington first took the oath of office on April 30, 1789." .
