  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "museum" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s8> <https://schema.org/url> <https://supremecourthistory.org/films/fdr-courtpacking-controversy-full-script/> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "National Archives" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "The Dred Scott Decision (American Originals)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s9> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "primary" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/s9> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.archives.gov/exhibits/american_originals/scott.html> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "Article III creates \"one supreme Court\" but sets no size; the Judiciary Act of 1789 gave it six justices, Congress changed the authorized number several times, and the figure of nine dates only from an 1869 statute." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The Constitution requires the Supreme Court to have nine justices." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Because nine has stood for more than 150 years, an ordinary act of Congress is easily mistaken for a constitutional rule." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why can Congress change the number of Supreme Court justices without amending the Constitution?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Article III creates \"one supreme Court\" but says nothing about its size, so the number is set by statute; the Judiciary Act of 1789 set six, and later laws moved it between five (never in effect) and ten before an 1869 act fixed it at nine." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did Marbury v. Madison expand the Court's role in the system of checks and balances?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Chief Justice John Marshall held that part of the Judiciary Act of 1789 conflicted with the Constitution and that courts must follow the Constitution when a statute conflicts with it, the first time the Court declared an act of Congress unconstitutional and the basis of judicial review." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did Franklin D. Roosevelt's 1937 plan to enlarge the Court fail?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Many saw it as a threat to judicial independence; a bipartisan Senate Judiciary Committee majority urged its emphatic rejection, the Court began upholding New Deal-era laws such as the minimum-wage law in West Coast Hotel v. Parrish, Justice Van Devanter retired, and the Senate defeated the plan on July 22, 1937." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How does most of the Court's work reach it, and how selective is it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Most cases arrive as petitions for a writ of certiorari asking the Court to review a lower-court decision; four justices must agree to take a case, and of up to about ten thousand requests a year the Court accepts fewer than 2 percent." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Congress reduces the authorized seats to seven, to be reached as vacancies occur." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1866-07-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Congress fixes the Court at nine justices, where it has remained." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1869-04-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Chief Justice Charles Evans Hughes lays the cornerstone of the Supreme Court Building." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1932-10-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Court moves into its own building in its 146th year." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1935"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "President Franklin D. Roosevelt asks Congress for up to six additional justices." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/14> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1937-02-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/15> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/15> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Court upholds a Washington State minimum-wage law for women in West Coast Hotel v. Parrish." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/15> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1937-03-29"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/16> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/16> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Roosevelt's plan to enlarge the Court is defeated in the Senate." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/16> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1937-07-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/17> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/17> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thurgood Marshall is sworn in as the first African American justice." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/17> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1967-10-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/18> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/18> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sandra Day O'Connor is sworn in as the first woman justice." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/18> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1981-09-25"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Judiciary Act of 1789 organizes the Court with a chief justice and five associate justices." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1789-09-24"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Court first convenes in the Exchange Building in New York City, a day late because some justices could not arrive in time." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1790-02-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/supreme-court-of-the-united-states/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Court issues its first opinion, in West v. Barnes." .
