  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/chinese-detention-barracks-poetry> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The body of poems, mostly in classical Chinese forms, that immigrants held under the Chinese exclusion laws brushed and carved into the wooden walls of the men's detention barracks at the Angel Island Immigration Station between 1910 and 1940, rediscovered in 1970 and now regarded as the first literary body of work by Chinese in North America." .
