  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/hip-hop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A youth culture and art form created by Black, Afro-Caribbean and Latino young people in the Bronx, New York City, in the early 1970s, combining DJing, MCing (rapping), breaking and graffiti, which grew from neighborhood parties into a music industry and a culture found across the United States and the world." .
