  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hoover Dam Monument Plaza" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hoover Dam Star Map" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/hoover-dam> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/public-art-in-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A pair of 30-foot bronze winged figures by the Norwegian-born sculptor Oskar J. W. Hansen, set on black diorite bases beside a 142-foot flagpole in a terrazzo plaza on the Nevada end of Hoover Dam, whose inlaid star map fixes the sky at the moment Franklin D. Roosevelt dedicated the dam on September 30, 1935." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/culture-and-arts> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/winged-figures-of-the-republic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Winged Figures of the Republic" .
