<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "The Bureau counts the population and applies a formula that Congress wrote into law (equal proportions, adopted in 1941); the states then redraw their own district lines using census redistricting data." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The Census Bureau decides how many House seats each state gets and draws the new congressional districts." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Because seat gains and losses are announced by the Census Bureau, the count, the formula and the separate state-run redistricting process are easily blurred together." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the original apportionment formula give slaveholding states extra representation, and how did that change?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Article I counted enslaved people as three-fifths of a person for apportionment though they could not vote, adding seats for slaveholding states; after emancipation the Fourteenth Amendment (1868) counted the whole number of persons, which would have fully counted freed people and so increased Southern power, which is why it added a never-enforced penalty for denying men the vote." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did Washington veto the first apportionment bill in 1792?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "He judged it unconstitutional because no single ratio produced its allotment and it gave eight states more than one representative per 30,000 people, the Constitution's limit." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the failure to reapportion after the 1920 census change the process?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Rural members, fearing a loss of power to fast-growing cities, blocked reapportionment for a decade; the 1929 act responded by making apportionment automatic after each census with the House kept at 435 seats." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What is the difference between apportionment and redistricting?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Apportionment divides the 435 House seats among the states by population; redistricting is each state's redrawing of district boundaries within its borders, using small-area counts the Census Bureau supplies." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Attorney General concludes that no American Indians remain 'not taxed' for census purposes." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1940"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Congress adopts the method of equal proportions for all future apportionments." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1941-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Department of Commerce v. Montana the Supreme Court upholds the equal-proportions method." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1992"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Census Bureau delivers 2020 apportionment counts; Texas gains two seats and seven states lose one." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2021-04-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Constitutional Convention votes to tie representation and direct taxes to population, counting enslaved people at three-fifths." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1787-07-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "U.S. marshals and their deputies begin the first federal census, which counts 3,929,214 people." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1790-08-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "George Washington casts the first presidential veto, rejecting a 120-seat apportionment bill as unconstitutional." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1792-04-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Washington signs a replacement act giving the House 105 seats under Jefferson's method." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1792-04-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Congress begins fixing the size of the House before apportionment and adopts the Vinton (Hamilton) method." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1850"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Fourteenth Amendment replaces the three-fifths formula with a count of the whole number of persons." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1868"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Congress fixes the House at 433 seats, plus one each for Arizona and New Mexico on statehood." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1911-08-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The census shows a shift to cities; Congress fails to reapportion for the only time." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1920"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Reapportionment and Census Act makes apportionment automatic after the 1930 census and keeps 435 seats." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment/timeline/9> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1929-06-18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Principle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Census and apportionment" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Apportionment of the House of Representatives" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Congressional apportionment" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Enumeration Clause" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Reapportionment of the House" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/united-states-congress> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The constitutional rule that seats in the U.S. House of Representatives are divided among the states by population, using an \"actual Enumeration\" of the people taken every ten years; it has been carried out after every census since 1790 except that of 1920." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/democracy-and-elections> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/census-and-apportionment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Census and apportionment" .
