  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "H-006-1: Battle of Midway — Overview" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "government" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s8> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.history.navy.mil/about-us/leadership/director/directors-corner/h-grams/h-gram-006/h-006-1.html> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "National Archives (Milestone Documents)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s9> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Lend-Lease Act (1941)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s9> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "primary" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/s9> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/lend-lease-act> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "The country was neutral in law but not in practice. From 1939 it sold arms to Britain and France on a cash-and-carry basis, in September 1940 it traded destroyers to Britain for bases, and from March 1941 the Lend-Lease Act let it supply Britain and other nations without immediate payment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The United States stayed strictly neutral in World War II until the attack on Pearl Harbor." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Pearl Harbor was such a sudden shock, and isolationist sentiment before it so loud, that the long, deliberate drift toward aiding the Allies is easily forgotten." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How was the United States involved in the war before Pearl Harbor even though it was officially neutral?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "It sold war materiel to Britain on a cash-and-carry basis from 1939, traded more than 50 destroyers to Britain for base leases in 1940, and under the March 1941 Lend-Lease Act supplied Britain and eventually more than 30 countries with about $50 billion in aid without demanding immediate payment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the United States end up fighting Germany as well as Japan after Pearl Harbor?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Congress declared war only on Japan on December 8, 1941. On December 11 Germany and Italy declared war on the United States, and Congress then passed resolutions recognizing a state of war with both." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did African American newspapers promote a \"Double V\" campaign during the war?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "About a million Black Americans served, mostly in segregated units led by white officers, while discrimination persisted at home; the Pittsburgh Courier's campaign urged victory over fascism abroad and over racism at home." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the war change the American economy and workforce?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Federal spending soared, unemployment virtually disappeared as some 20 million workers entered the military, women took over a million administrative jobs and became a majority of aircraft-industry workers by 1943, and the bracero program brought Mexican laborers to fill farm jobs." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "American combat troops land in French Morocco, opening the campaign in North Africa." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1942-11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "D-Day: almost 133,000 Allied troops land on five Normandy beaches under General Eisenhower's command." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1944-06-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Berlin falls days after Hitler's suicide, and Americans celebrate V-E Day." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1945-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A U.S. atomic bomb destroys Hiroshima; a second bomb strikes Nagasaki on August 9." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1945-08-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Japan signs the Instrument of Surrender aboard USS Missouri in Tokyo Bay." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/14> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1945-09-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "War breaks out in Europe; Roosevelt declares the United States neutral in law, and a new Neutrality Act lets warring nations buy American arms only on a cash-and-carry basis." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1939-09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Roosevelt signs the destroyers-for-bases agreement, trading more than 50 old destroyers to Britain for 99-year leases on bases in Newfoundland and the Caribbean." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1940-09-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Lend-Lease Act is approved, letting the President sell, lend or lease war materiel to any country whose defense he deems vital to U.S. defense." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1941-03-11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Japan attacks the U.S. fleet and airfields at Pearl Harbor, Hawaiʻi." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1941-12-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Congress declares war on Japan, 82-0 in the Senate and 388-1 in the House." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1941-12-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
