  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "United States in World War II" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The American part in the Second World War, from formal neutrality and aid to Britain after 1939, through belligerency against Japan, Germany and Italy from December 1941, to Japan's surrender aboard USS Missouri on September 2, 1945 — a war that mobilized more than 12 million Americans in uniform at its peak and remade the home front." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/depression-and-world-war> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/world-war-ii-and-the-united-states> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "World War II and the United States" .
