  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Forty-Niners' gold rush" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Gold Rush of 1848–1855" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Gold Rush of 1849" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/history-of-california> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/territorial-expansion-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mass migration to California set off when James Marshall found gold at John Sutter's sawmill on the American River on January 24, 1848; it drew some 300,000 people from across the world by the mid-1850s, sped California to statehood as a free state in 1850, enriched merchants more than most miners, and brought dispossession, forced labor and mass death to Native Californians and discriminatory taxes on foreign miners." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/early-republic-and-expansion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/california-gold-rush> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "California Gold Rush" .
