  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Federal minimum wage" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Minimum wage in the United States" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Minimum wage laws" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/labor-history-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/labor-law-in-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The legal floor on hourly pay in the United States, first adopted by the states for women workers beginning with Massachusetts in 1912 and set nationally by the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, which fixed a federal minimum of 25 cents an hour; the federal rate has been $7.25 since July 24, 2009, while most states set higher rates of their own." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/economy-and-work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/minimum-wage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Minimum wage" .
