  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "The American Presidency Project, University of California, Santa Barbara" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s5> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Statement on the National Business and Economic Situation (Herbert Hoover, October 25, 1929)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "primary" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s5> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/statement-the-national-business-and-economic-situation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "The Saturday Evening Post (Jeff Nilsson, October 29, 2019)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "6 Myths about the Stock Market Crash of 1929" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "magazine" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/stock-market-crash-of-1929/s6> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.saturdayeveningpost.com/2019/10/6-myths-about-the-stock-market-crash-of-1929/> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "Only about 3 million of roughly 120 million Americans, under 2.5 percent, owned any stock in 1929, most of them in small holdings; the widespread ruin came later, as banks failed and jobs disappeared during the Depression." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "Most Americans had their savings in the stock market, so the crash ruined ordinary families across the country at a stroke." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "The crash is remembered through the Depression that followed, so the hardship of the 1930s is often projected back onto a few days of trading that directly touched a small minority." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did buying on margin make the crash worse once prices began to fall?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Investors had paid only part of a share's price and borrowed the rest against the shares, an arrangement that worked only while prices kept rising; once prices fell, the borrowed positions could not be sustained, and panic selling drove prices down further." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why do many economists say the crash did not by itself cause the Great Depression?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The economy had already begun contracting in the summer of 1929, the crash's effects on spending faded within months and recovery looked likely by fall 1930, and it was later problems in the financial system, above all bank failures, that turned a recession into a depression; some, like Allan Meltzer, call the crash a symptom of the downturn rather than a cause." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the crash change federal regulation of Wall Street?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "It led the Senate to investigate stock exchange practices; the Pecora hearings exposed questionable dealings such as Charles Mitchell's tax-avoiding stock sale and built support for the Banking Act of 1933, which separated commercial from investment banking and created deposit insurance, and the Securities Exchange Act of 1934." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "By mid-November the Dow has lost almost half its value." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1929-11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Senate authorizes its Banking and Currency Committee to investigate stock exchange practices." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1932-03-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Dow bottoms at 41.22, about 89 percent below its 1929 peak." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1932-07-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Roosevelt signs the Securities Exchange Act of 1934." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1934-06-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Dow finally regains its 1929 high." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/14> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1954-11-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/stock-market-crash-of-1929/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Dow Jones Industrial Average stands at 63." .
