  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/triangle-shirtwaist-factory-fire> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/progressive-era> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/triangle-shirtwaist-factory-fire> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fire at the Triangle Waist Company on the top three floors of the Asch Building in New York City on March 25, 1911, that killed 146 garment workers, most of them young immigrant women from southern and eastern Europe, and spurred New York's Factory Investigating Commission and a wave of state workplace-safety and labor laws." .
