  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/good-neighbor-policy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/foreign-relations-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/good-neighbor-policy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The U.S. approach to Latin America and the Caribbean that President Franklin D. Roosevelt announced in his inaugural address of March 4, 1933, renouncing armed intervention in the hemisphere in favor of cooperation and trade; it built on steps taken under Herbert Hoover and was followed by the withdrawal of U.S. forces from Haiti and the end of the U.S. treaty right to intervene in Cuba." .
