<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "Article 5 treats an attack on one as an attack on all, but each member takes \"such action as it deems necessary,\" which may or may not include armed force; U.S. negotiators insisted on that wording because the Constitution gives Congress the power to declare war." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "Article 5 automatically obliges every NATO member to go to war when an ally is attacked." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "The slogan \"an attack on one is an attack on all\" is remembered without the clause that leaves each government to decide its own response." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the United States refuse to write an automatic military commitment into the North Atlantic Treaty?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "European negotiators wanted a guarantee of automatic U.S. intervention, but under the Constitution only Congress can declare war, so Article 5 lets each member take the action it deems necessary, including but not limited to armed force." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the Vandenberg Resolution prepare the way for NATO?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Adopted by the Senate in June 1948, it endorsed U.S. association with regional collective-defense arrangements under the UN Charter and through constitutional processes, giving the administration bipartisan Senate backing to negotiate the treaty." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why was joining NATO a break with earlier American foreign policy?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "It was the first peacetime military alliance the United States entered outside the Western Hemisphere, ending a long tradition of avoiding alliances with European powers." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What did the only invocation of Article 5 lead to?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "After the September 11, 2001, attacks the allies invoked Article 5 on September 12; NATO then agreed eight support measures and sent AWACS radar planes to patrol U.S. skies in Operation Eagle Assist, its first Article 5 operation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "West Germany joins; the Soviet Union answers with its own alliance of Eastern European states, the Warsaw Pact." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1955"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "After eight days of debate, the Senate approves the accession of Poland, Hungary and the Czech Republic, 80 to 19." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1998-04-30"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "NATO invokes Article 5 for the first time, the day after the September 11 attacks on the United States." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2001-09-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sweden becomes the 32nd member." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2024-03-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Britain, France, Belgium, the Netherlands and Luxembourg sign the Brussels Treaty, a five-nation collective defense pact." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1948-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Senate adopts the Vandenberg Resolution, backing U.S. association with regional collective-defense arrangements through constitutional processes." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1948-06-11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Twelve nations sign the North Atlantic Treaty in Washington; Secretary of State Dean Acheson signs for the United States." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1949-04-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Senate Foreign Relations Committee reports the treaty favorably by a vote of 13 to 0." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/nato/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1949-06-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
