<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "It was a separate statement made more than eighty years later, in Theodore Roosevelt's December 1904 message to Congress. The 1823 doctrine asked European powers to stay out of the hemisphere; the corollary claimed a right for the United States itself to intervene." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The Roosevelt Corollary was simply part of the Monroe Doctrine as announced in 1823." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Roosevelt presented his policy as an extension of Monroe's, and the two are usually taught together, so the later claim of a U.S. police power is easily read back into 1823." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did a crisis over Venezuela's debts prompt Roosevelt to rethink the Monroe Doctrine?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The 1902 European blockade of Venezuela showed that European powers would use force to collect debts in the Americas; Roosevelt feared such actions could become invasions, so he claimed a U.S. right to step in first and make sure creditors were paid." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the corollary turn the Monroe Doctrine's meaning around?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Monroe's 1823 doctrine was a largely passive warning to Europeans not to intervene in the hemisphere, while the corollary justified U.S. intervention, including later occupations of Haiti and the Dominican Republic." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the Dominican customs receivership show the corollary in practice?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "A U.S.-appointed receiver collected Dominican customs duties and applied them to receivership costs and a refinanced debt before passing the rest to the Dominican government, which could not raise its debt or change tariffs without U.S. agreement." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did Roosevelt use executive agreements in the Dominican case?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Critics said his January 1905 agreement bypassed the Senate, and when Democratic opposition blocked a treaty, he put the receivership into effect by a modus vivendi until the Senate approved a convention in 1907." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "At the Montevideo conference the United States pledges non-intervention in the hemisphere." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1933"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Franklin D. Roosevelt's Good Neighbor policy officially abandons the corollary." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1934"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "James Monroe's annual message warns European powers against new colonization or intervention in the Americas." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1823-12-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "British, German and Italian warships blockade Venezuela's ports after it defaults on debts to foreign bondholders." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1902"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Theodore Roosevelt announces the corollary in his annual message to Congress." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1904-12-06"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A U.S.-Dominican executive agreement gives the United States control of Dominican customhouses; critics say it bypasses the Senate." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1905-01-20"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "With Senate action on a treaty blocked, Roosevelt puts a customs receivership into effect by a modus vivendi." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1905-04-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/roosevelt-corollary/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The United States and the Dominican Republic sign a convention at Santo Domingo making the receivership formal." .
