  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/bureau-of-ocean-energy-management> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "BOEM" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/bureau-of-ocean-energy-management> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "U.S. Bureau of Ocean Energy Management" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/bureau-of-ocean-energy-management> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/department-of-the-interior> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/bureau-of-ocean-energy-management> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Department of the Interior bureau, formally established on October 1, 2011, out of the breakup of the Minerals Management Service after the Deepwater Horizon oil spill, that leases and plans the development of oil, gas, wind and marine minerals on the roughly 3.2 billion acres of the U.S. Outer Continental Shelf." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/bureau-of-ocean-energy-management> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/geography-and-environment> .
