  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/chesapeake-bay> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The largest estuary in the United States, a drowned river valley about 190 miles long between Maryland and Virginia whose 64,000-square-mile watershed reaches into six states and the District of Columbia; homeland of Algonquian-speaking and other Native nations, the setting of English colonization, slavery's tobacco economy and decisive battles of two wars, and the object of a decades-long federal–state cleanup." .
