<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "Negotiators relied on only about 20 years of gauge records; a 1976 tree-ring reconstruction put the 1564–1961 average at about 13.5 million acre-feet a year and found 1905–1930 the wettest such period in 400 years, while the Compact and the 1944 treaty together assigned up to 17.5 million." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The 1922 Colorado River Compact divided a river whose long-term average flow was well known." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "The Compact's fixed numbers look like measurements, but they rest on an unusually wet stretch of record, which is a root of today's shortages." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the 1922 Compact divide the river at Lee Ferry rather than state by state, and what did it promise each side?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Herbert Hoover proposed splitting the basin into an Upper and a Lower half; the Compact gave each 7.5 million acre-feet a year (the Lower Basin could add 1 million more) and required the Upper Division not to deplete the flow at Lee Ferry below 75 million acre-feet over any ten years. The Lower Basin's share was divided among Arizona, California and Nevada later, by the 1928 Boulder Canyon Project Act." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How do tree-ring studies help explain the Colorado River's modern water shortages?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "They show the Compact was based on an unusually wet period (1905–1930), so the long-term flow (about 13.5 million acre-feet a year in one reconstruction) is far below the 16.5 million acre-feet promised to the two basins plus 1.5 million to Mexico." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How were Native nations' water rights treated in the Compact and later recognized?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "No tribe took part in the 1922 negotiations, and the Compact only said it did not affect U.S. obligations to tribes; in Arizona v. California (1963) the Supreme Court applied the 1908 Winters doctrine and held that five lower-river reservations had reserved enough water to irrigate their practicably irrigable land." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Bureau of Reclamation declares the first shortage in Lake Mead's history, cutting 2022 deliveries to Arizona, Nevada and Mexico." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2021-08-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hopi guides lead a party under García López de Cárdenas, part of Coronado's expedition, to the rim of the Grand Canyon." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1540"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Domínguez–Escalante expedition fords the river at the Crossing of the Fathers, now beneath Lake Powell." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1776"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The federal government establishes the Colorado River Reservation for the Mohave and Chemehuevi peoples." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1865"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "John Wesley Powell's expedition launches four boats at Green River, Wyoming; it leaves the Grand Canyon on August 28." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1869-05-24"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Representatives of seven states and the federal government sign the Colorado River Compact at Santa Fe, New Mexico." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1922-11-24"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Boulder Canyon Project Act approves the Compact, authorizes Hoover Dam and divides the Lower Basin's share among Arizona, California and Nevada." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1928"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A water treaty with Mexico commits 1.5 million acre-feet a year of the river's flow to Mexico." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1944"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Arizona v. California the Supreme Court settles the Lower Basin division and recognizes reserved water rights for five reservations." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1963"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/colorado-river/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A pulse flow under Minute 319 of the 1944 treaty begins; it eventually reaches the river's estuary in the Gulf of California." .
