<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "The Court never reached the merits; it dismissed the suit because it lacked jurisdiction, while describing the Cherokee Nation as a distinct political society capable of governing itself. A year later Worcester v. Georgia held Georgia's laws void inside the Nation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "In Cherokee Nation v. Georgia the Supreme Court upheld Georgia's laws and ruled that the Cherokee Nation had no sovereignty." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Because the Cherokees lost the case and were later forcibly removed, the jurisdictional dismissal is easily remembered as a ruling on Georgia's power or a denial of Cherokee nationhood." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the Supreme Court refuse to hear the Cherokee Nation's suit against Georgia?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The Constitution lets the Court hear suits between a state and foreign states, and the majority held that the Cherokee Nation, though a distinct political society, was not a foreign state but a domestic dependent nation, partly because the commerce clause lists foreign nations, states and Indian tribes as separate categories; without jurisdiction it had to dismiss the case." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the 1831 dismissal help set up Worcester v. Georgia?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Marshall suggested the land question might be decided in a proper case with proper parties, and when Georgia convicted missionaries such as Samuel Worcester under its license law, their appeal from a state court gave the Supreme Court jurisdiction to rule that Georgia's laws had no force in the Cherokee Nation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why is the case's guardian-and-ward language still important in federal Indian law?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Marshall's description of the tribes' relation to the United States as resembling that of a ward to its guardian became a root of the federal trust responsibility, the duty the federal government owes tribes to protect their remaining lands and provide services." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Cherokee Nation adopts a written constitution modeled on the U.S. Constitution." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1827"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Georgia declares the Cherokee government abolished and places Cherokee citizens under state law; gold is found on Cherokee land in the north Georgia mountains." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1828"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "President Andrew Jackson signs the Indian Removal Act." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1830-05-28"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Cherokee Nation's motion for an injunction against Georgia is set for hearing before the Supreme Court; Georgia does not appear." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1831-03-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Court denies the injunction and dismisses the Cherokee Nation's bill for want of jurisdiction." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1831-03-18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In Worcester v. Georgia the Court holds that Georgia's laws have no force within the Cherokee Nation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1832"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A small Cherokee faction without authority under Cherokee law signs the Treaty of New Echota." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1835"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "President Martin Van Buren orders General Winfield Scott to remove the remaining Cherokees, beginning the Trail of Tears." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1838-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/cherokee-nation-v-georgia> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#CourtCase> .
