  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/dawes-act> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The federal law signed by President Grover Cleveland on February 8, 1887, that authorized the president to divide reservation land held in common by Native nations into individual allotments, held in trust for twenty-five years, and to sell the remaining \"surplus\" to non-Indians; by 1934, when the policy ended, land held by Native people had fallen from about 138 million acres to 48 million." .
