  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/susan-b-anthony> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Quaker-raised reformer (1820–1906) from Massachusetts and Rochester, New York, who worked for temperance and abolition, co-led the National Woman Suffrage Association with Elizabeth Cady Stanton, was convicted in 1873 of voting illegally, and campaigned for a federal woman suffrage amendment that was ratified fourteen years after her death as the Nineteenth Amendment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/susan-b-anthony> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/people-who-shaped-america> .
