  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/benjamin-franklin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Boston-born Philadelphia printer, writer, scientist and civic organizer (1706–1790) who became a colonial agent in London, a member of the Continental Congress, the first American minister received by a foreign government, a delegate to the Constitutional Convention and, after decades of owning enslaved people, president of Pennsylvania's antislavery society." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/benjamin-franklin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/presidents-and-founders> .
