  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/theodore-roosevelt> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The 26th president of the United States (1901–1909), a New York Republican who took office at 42 after William McKinley's assassination, regulated big business under his \"Square Deal,\" protected about 230 million acres of public land, won the 1906 Nobel Peace Prize, and ran for president again in 1912 as a Progressive." .
