  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/detroit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Michigan city and the state's first capital, founded by the French in 1701 as Fort Pontchartrain du détroit on Anishinaabe land along the Detroit River; it became the center of the American automobile industry and the \"arsenal of democracy\" in World War II, a major destination of Black southern migrants, and later a symbol of deindustrialization, urban decline and the largest municipal bankruptcy in U.S. history (2013)." .
