  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/gatun-locks> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Gatún Locks" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/gatun-locks> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/panama-canal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/gatun-locks> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The three-step flight of paired lock chambers at the Atlantic end of the Panama Canal, built by the United States between 1909 and 1913, which uses gravity-fed water from Gatun Lake to raise and lower ships about 85 feet between the Caribbean Sea and the lake." .
