  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/the-west> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The western part of the United States, defined by the Census Bureau as a 13-state region of Mountain and Pacific divisions; a largely arid land of Native homelands and former Mexican territory that the United States conquered and settled in the nineteenth century, where the federal government still owns much of the land, and whose meaning historians have long debated." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/the-west> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/regions-cities-and-landmarks> .
