  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/due-process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Due Process Clauses" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/due-process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Due process of law" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/due-process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/bill-of-rights> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/due-process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/due-process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The constitutional guarantee, in the Fifth Amendment (binding the federal government) and the Fourteenth Amendment (binding the states), that no person may be deprived of life, liberty, or property without due process of law: fair procedures such as notice and a hearing, and, as the courts have read it, some protection for fundamental rights as well." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/due-process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/rights-and-law> .
