  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "1 Cranch 137" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "5 U.S. 137" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Marbury case" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Marbury et al. v. Madison" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Marbury v Madison" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/judicial-review> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The February 1803 U.S. Supreme Court decision in which Chief Justice John Marshall held that William Marbury was legally entitled to his undelivered commission as a District of Columbia justice of the peace, but that the Court could not order it delivered because the provision of the Judiciary Act of 1789 it would have relied on unconstitutionally enlarged the Court's original jurisdiction; it was the first time the Court treated an act of Congress as void." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/rights-and-law> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/marbury-v-madison> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Marbury v. Madison" .
