<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "The arrays are far too small to be seen from Earth; scientists find them only by the laser light they send back, and spacecraft cameras in lunar orbit are what have pinpointed their positions to within a metre." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "Telescopes on Earth can see the reflectors and other equipment the Apollo astronauts left on the Moon." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Because observatories aim lasers at the reflectors every night, it is easy to assume astronomers can simply look at them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How does bouncing a laser off a mirror on the Moon measure the Earth–Moon distance?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Corner-cube prisms send light straight back toward its source, so scientists time how long a laser pulse takes to make the roughly 2.5-second round trip and convert that time into distance." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the Apollo 11 experiment become far more precise over the following decades, even though the reflector never changed?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The reflector needs no power, so better lasers, timing electronics and larger telescopes on Earth could keep improving the measurement — from an uncertainty of about 5 metres in August 1969 to about 2 centimetres by 1999 and about a millimetre with APOLLO." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What has lunar laser ranging revealed about the Moon and about gravity?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "It shows the Moon receding about 3.8 cm a year because of tides, indicates the Moon has a fluid core, measures how tides flex the Moon, and finds that the Sun pulls on Earth and Moon alike despite their different makeup, a test of Einstein's theory of gravity." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why was the experiment also a Cold War race?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Soviet scientists were also firing lasers at the Moon, and the U.S. sponsors urged American teams to get the first returns before the Soviets did." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The APOLLO project at Apache Point Observatory, New Mexico, begins ranging with millimetre-level precision." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2005-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IEEE dedicates a milestone plaque at Lick Observatory for the 1969 experiment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2019-08-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Discussions in Princeton's experimental gravitation research group plant the idea of ranging to a reflector on the Moon." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1960"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
