  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lunar-laser-ranging-experiment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The scientific experiment begun when Apollo 11's astronauts set a panel of 100 glass corner-cube reflectors on the Moon in July 1969; observatories on Earth have timed laser pulses bounced off it and later reflectors ever since, measuring the Earth–Moon distance from metres in 1969 to about a millimetre today." .
