  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/telegraph> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The system of sending coded messages as pulses of electric current over wires, which Samuel F. B. Morse and his collaborators demonstrated between Washington and Baltimore in 1844 and which grew into the first nationwide electrical communications industry, dominated after 1866 by Western Union." .
