  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s7> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.archives.gov/press/press-releases/2016/nr16-52.html> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "Library of Congress, Manuscript Division" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Huffman Prairie — Wilbur and Orville Wright Papers, Collection Highlights" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#sourceType> "primary" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/source/wright-brothers-first-flight/s8> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.loc.gov/collections/wilbur-and-orville-wright-papers/articles-and-essays/collection-highlights/huffman-prairie/> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "The flights took off from the sand dunes at Kill Devil Hills, about four miles south of the village of Kitty Hawk; the brothers walked to Kitty Hawk afterwards to send the telegram announcing their success." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The Wright brothers first flew in the town of Kitty Hawk." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Kitty Hawk was the nearest village — its weather station first invited the brothers and their telegram was sent from there — so its name travelled with the news." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did two Ohio bicycle makers test their aircraft on the North Carolina Outer Banks?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "They wanted steady winds, hills, soft sand and few trees; of the weather stations they wrote to, only Kitty Hawk replied, and its weatherman Bill Tate offered to host them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the flight of December 17, 1903, differ from earlier hops and glides by other experimenters?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Others had glided or lifted off briefly, but the Wrights' Flyer took off under its own engine power and flew in sustained flight under the pilot's complete control — the first such demonstration of a heavier-than-air machine." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the 1903 Flyer spend twenty years outside the Smithsonian?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "After Langley's death the Smithsonian displayed his rebuilt Aerodrome as the first airplane capable of sustained flight, based on modified 1914 tests by Glenn Curtiss; Orville sent the Flyer to London in protest and it returned only after the Smithsonian published a correction in 1942, arriving in 1948." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Amid a feud with the Smithsonian, Orville ships the 1903 Flyer to the Science Museum in London." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1928"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Flyer is installed at the Smithsonian, 45 years to the day after it flew." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1948-12-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Wrights begin testing gliders on the Outer Banks near Kitty Hawk, whose weather station had answered their inquiry about steady winds and open sand." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1900"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wilbur glides 622 feet in 21 seconds, setting American distance and time records for gliders." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1902-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The brothers file their patent application for a \"Flying-Machine\"." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1903-03-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Samuel Langley's Smithsonian-backed Great Aerodrome crashes on its second launch attempt." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/wright-brothers-first-flight/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1903-12-08"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
