  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/gullah-geechee> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The African American people of the lower Atlantic coast and Sea Islands, from North Carolina to northeast Florida, descended from West and Central Africans enslaved on rice, indigo and Sea Island cotton plantations, whose relative isolation preserved a distinctive creole language and many African-rooted traditions." .
