  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/betsy-ross-flag-myth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The popular story that Philadelphia upholsterer Betsy Ross designed and sewed the first Stars and Stripes at George Washington's request in 1776, a family tradition first made public by her grandson in 1870 that no contemporary document supports." .
