  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Symbol> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "E pluribus unum" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "E Pluribus Unum" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Motto of the Great Seal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Out of many, one" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/national-symbols-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Latin motto \"E pluribus unum\" (\"Out of many, one\"), first proposed for a national seal in August 1776 and adopted on the Great Seal of the United States in 1782, where it refers to the union of the states; federal law still requires it on U.S. coins, though it was never designated the national motto." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/symbols-and-national-identity> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/e-pluribus-unum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "E pluribus unum" .
